---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Field Survey & Outbreak Audit | Pharos University">
	<style>
		.article-nav {
			padding: 24px 60px;
			border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-grid);
			display: flex;
			justify-content: space-between;
			align-items: center;
		}

		.article-body {
			max-width: 800px;
			margin: 60px auto;
			padding: 0 24px;
			line-height: 1.8;
			font-size: 16px;
		}

		.article-eyebrow {
			font-family: var(--font-mono);
			font-size: 12px;
			font-weight: 800;
			color: var(--accent-critical);
			letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		}

		.article-headline {
			font-size: 38px;
			font-weight: 900;
			margin: 16px 0 24px;
			line-height: 1.15;
		}

		.article-meta {
			font-family: var(--font-mono);
			font-size: 12px;
			color: var(--text-muted);
			border-top: 1px solid var(--border-grid);
			border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-grid);
			padding: 16px 0;
			margin-bottom: 40px;
		}

		.callout-box {
			background: var(--bg-muted);
			border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-critical);
			padding: 24px;
			margin: 32px 0;
			font-size: 15px;
		}
	</style>

	<header class="article-nav">
		<a href="/blog" style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent-blue); text-decoration: none;">&larr; BACK TO RESEARCH BLOG</a>
		<span style="font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-muted);">PHAROS UNIVERSITY GRADUATION PROJECT Proposal Section 2.1 & 2.2</span>
	</header>

	<main class="article-body">
		<div class="article-eyebrow">CLINICAL AUDIT ARTICLE</div>
		<h1 class="article-headline">London & Seoul Dialysis Unit Outbreaks: Field Survey & Chloramine Neglect Patterns</h1>
		
		<div class="article-meta">
			AUTHORS: Aya Anwer, Ahmed Nassar, Amr Khaled, Ahmed Gamal, Abdelrahman Seif, Shaza Hany  
			<br />SUPERVISION: Dr. Mohamed Abdou, Office of the Dean | Pharos University in Alexandria
		</div>

		<p>
			Dialysis unit outbreaks historically stem from a single shared vulnerability: unrecorded, gradual degradation of water treatment loops. In London, Hard Water Syndrome exposed 30 patients to hypercalcemia when softener resin failed silently. In Seoul, Chloramine Hemolysis caused an 83% attack rate due to unmonitored carbon tank breakthrough.
		</p>

		<div class="callout-box">
			<strong>Field Audit Key Finding:</strong> Field surveys conducted at partner hemodialysis units in Alexandria confirmed that chloramine testing neglect recurred over 60 times in a single year due to clerical paper chart overhead.
		</div>

		<h2 style="font-size: 22px; font-weight: 800; margin: 32px 0 16px;">The Role of Continuous IoT Telemetry</h2>
		<p>
			By embedding point-of-care IoT probes directly into the dialysate feed and water treatment loops, our framework shifts unit monitoring from once-daily manual paper logs to continuous 60 FPS sensor telemetry—recovering 20 missing data days per year and eliminating clerical blindspots.
		</p>
	</main>
</Layout>
